"<p><strong>SaaSBase</strong> is a modern, self-hosted PaaS (Platform as a Service) and BaaS (Backend as a Service) deployer designed for developers, DevOps engineers, and teams who want total control over their infrastructure without the complexity of Kubernetes.</p>\n<p>Connect any Linux VPS over SSH or run SaaSBase directly on the host machine. SaaSBase configures Docker and Traefik v3, provisions SSL certificates, and allows you to deploy popular open-source platforms like <strong>Supabase</strong>, <strong>PocketBase</strong>, <strong>Appwrite</strong>, and <strong>n8n</strong> from templates or your own Git repositories.</p>\n<h2>Comparison Matrix</h2>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th align=\"left\">Feature</th><th align=\"left\">SaaSBase</th><th align=\"left\">Coolify</th><th align=\"left\">Dokploy</th><th align=\"left\">CapRover</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Primary Focus</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Secure PaaS + Native Supabase Ecosystem</td><td align=\"left\">Full PaaS Alternative to Heroku</td><td align=\"left\">Lightweight Docker PaaS</td><td align=\"left\">Docker Swarm PaaS</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Reverse Proxy</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Traefik v3</strong> (Native dynamic routing)</td><td align=\"left\">Traefik</td><td align=\"left\">Traefik</td><td align=\"left\">NGINX</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Zero-Trust Network</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Cloudflare Tunnel (Tunnel-Only)</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Community Workaround</td><td align=\"left\">Community Workaround</td><td align=\"left\">NGINX Plugin</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Secret Encryption</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>AES-256-CBC + HKDF (v2)</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Basic Encryption</td><td align=\"left\">Basic Encryption</td><td align=\"left\">Plain / Basic</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Disaster Recovery</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Built-in Split-Brain Guard + Offsite S3/R2</td><td align=\"left\">S3 Backup</td><td align=\"left\">S3 Backup</td><td align=\"left\">Backup archive</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Cloud Import</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Supabase Cloud Sync (DB + Storage + Functions)</strong></td><td align=\"left\">No</td><td align=\"left\">No</td><td align=\"left\">No</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Runtime &#x26; Tech Stack</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Bun + React 19 + TanStack Start</strong></td><td align=\"left\">PHP / Laravel</td><td align=\"left\">Node.js / Next.js</td><td align=\"left\">Node.js</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>System Requirements</h2>\n<h3>Recommended Server Specs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Operating System:</strong> Ubuntu 22.04 / 24.04 LTS, Debian 11 / 12 (amd64 or arm64 architecture).</li>\n<li><strong>CPU:</strong> 1 Core minimum (2+ Cores recommended for Supabase or build jobs).</li>\n<li><strong>Memory (RAM):</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>1 GB minimum for SaaSBase core + lightweight apps (PocketBase, SQLite).</li>\n<li>2 GB to 4 GB recommended for the complete Supabase stack.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Storage:</strong> 20 GB SSD minimum.</li>\n<li><strong>Ports (Standard Mode):</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Port <code>22</code> (SSH)</li>\n<li>Port <code>80</code> &#x26; <code>443</code> (HTTP/HTTPS via Traefik)</li>\n<li>Port <code>3000</code> (SaaSBase Web Panel, can be bound to localhost)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"docCallout docCallout-tip\"><div class=\"docCalloutHeader\"><span class=\"docCalloutBadge\">TIP</span><span class=\"docCalloutTitle\">Tunnel-Only Advantage</span></div><div class=\"docCalloutContent\">\n<p>When operating servers via <strong>Cloudflare Tunnel</strong>, ports <code>80</code> and <code>443</code> can remain <strong>completely closed</strong> on your server firewall!</p>\n</div></div>"